From b5ebef2c2c5d229e2a9079b67ae11f6c58836eac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:48:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] refactor(server): one seat resolver, NO_STORE and the
 answers, one body reader, the result router, types

R1.3.4: seatAnswer (src/lib/routes/seat-resolver.ts) answers every seat route: the session (401),
then its address, then its seat (404), then its responder. The 21 route files are each one call
to it. getPlayerSeat sits beside getGmSeat in db/seats; the four companion seat helpers stay by
name (companion-routes.integration.test calls each) on those two, and the party's player seat is
partyAt beside its responders, so no route's import closure grows (the GM routes suite mocks
db/seats with getGmSeat alone; route suites mock db/table without what db/companions reads). The two
texts/[hash] routes keep their header quirks (B16): NO_HEADERS on the player's 401 and 404s and
the Gamemaster's 401. notesSeat reads the player's seat by getPlayerSeat, its stricter check
kept.

R1.3.5: src/lib/routes/http.ts: NO_STORE (the 25 files' constant), bare, textAnswer (3 copies)
and seenAs for the five 204 checks: numbers, text and flags as each compared them, and what a page
may leave out (gm, gmrolls) by its absence. Every answer keeps its headers and Content-Type.

R1.3.6: readBody (src/lib/routes/body.ts) for the five readers, each mapping why to today's
answer: rolls 415/413/400 bare, notes 415 bare and 413/400 `{reason: 'invalid'}`, dishes the
type lower-cased and the declared size first, events and commands the declared size first; the
two that never checked a declared size still don't (B4).

R1.3.7: recordCommandResult routes dish-, roll and note results; a roll's marks are
markGmMessages and closeAnsweredPrompt, then the version bump, the same writes in the same
order.

R1.3.12: S's exported types to src/db/types.ts (the notes', note-sync's, cookbook's, PartySeat,
CompanionStatus, CampaignStatus, EventCampaign, Tx once), src/lib/routes/types.ts (NotesPlace,
NotesAddress, Refusal, and the new helpers' types) and src/lib/types.ts (SessionUser); the
three util *Refusal types un-exported. Importers, tests' import lines included, follow.

L1 (l1/S/c10b, on this tree over a2332a2 with commit 9): jest 305 suites, 9689 tests, 0 red;
typegen, tsc 0 errors; eslint 0 errors, 625 warnings; gates 1-12 ok (gate 9 625 against 981,
gate 12 two cycle groups, base four).

